{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Ub18uSdfHQcviRXk7cT66S","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CSyncmers\n2\t\n3\tClosed syncmers in pure C. Supports arbitrary k values and s < 64 (using `uint128_t`). s-mers are selected according to lexicographic order. Achieves around 60 MB/sec throughput.\n4\t\n5\t\n6\t\n7\t\n8\t### Some of existing code\n9\t\n10\tStrobealign code: uses 64-bit smers \n11\thttps://github.com/ksahlin/strobealign/blob/71866c31b578e5166c83aaf1fde79d238246490d/src/randstrobes.cpp#L57\n12\t\n13\tMinimap2 code: uses 64-bit smers\n14\thttps://github.com/lh3/minimap2/blob/c2f07ff2ac8bdc5c6768e63191e614ea9012bd5d/sketch.c#L145-L192\n15\t\n16\tCuriouscoding blog:\n17\thttps://curiouscoding.nl/posts/fast-minimizers/\n18\t\n19\tSliding window minimum algorithm explanation:\n20\thttps://github.com/keegancsmith/Sliding-Window-Minimum?tab=readme-ov-file#sliding-window-minimum-algorithm\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7afcba77-8e0d-481b-8c5d-ae5fd4c0d979","uuid":"6b98f3a3-8250-4b38-a0de-83c8790c7d00","timestamp":"2026-06-05T23:31:15.517Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-31062124/harvest-crust-D1ZOmw/project/c_src/README.md","content":"# CSyncmers\n\nClosed syncmers in pure C. Supports arbitrary k values and s < 64 (using `uint128_t`). s-mers are selected according to lexicographic order. Achieves around 60 MB/sec throughput.\n\n\n\n\n### Some of existing code\n\nStrobealign code: uses 64-bit smers \nhttps://github.com/ksahlin/strobealign/blob/71866c31b578e5166c83aaf1fde79d238246490d/src/randstrobes.cpp#L57\n\nMinimap2 code: uses 64-bit smers\nhttps://github.com/lh3/minimap2/blob/c2f07ff2ac8bdc5c6768e63191e614ea9012bd5d/sketch.c#L145-L192\n\nCuriouscoding blog:\nhttps://curiouscoding.nl/posts/fast-minimizers/\n\nSliding window minimum algorithm explanation:\nhttps://github.com/keegancsmith/Sliding-Window-Minimum?tab=readme-ov-file#sliding-window-minimum-algorithm\n","n